  "title": "Semantic Role",
  "definition": "The semantic relationship between a participant and the event or state described by the predicate. Common semantic roles include [term:agent], [term:patient], and [term:theme]. Semantic roles are distinct from grammatical relations: the [term:subject] of a passive clause is typically a [term:patient], not an [term:agent].",
